│ - If a port is in use, **USE A DIFFERENT PORT** instead of killing the proce │
│ ss using it                                                                  │
│ - Check what's running on a port with `lsof -i :<port>` or `ss -tlnp | grep  │
│ <port>`                                                                      │
│ - Prefer random/high ports (e.g., `docker run -p 0:8080`) to avoid conflicts │
│                                                                              │
│ **General Safety:**                                                          │
│ - **NEVER** run commands that affect system-wide state unless explicitly req │
│ uired by the PRD                                                             │
